From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DenialOfGravity <DenialOfGravity@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] redfin 1262: composite a swap's layers (kern.sweet_present_layers)

The SwapEnd record is IOMFB's swap record (Asahi's struct dcp_swap): per layer the surface id (0x54), source rect
(0x64), surface flags (0xa4, 0xb4), destination rect (0xc4); the layers this swap sets (0x104). A layer the mask does
not name keeps its surface. Photos' All Photos has two live full-screen layers (l0 the grid, l1 backboardd's frame with
transparent holes); CA sends 0x7 then 0x2 (only l1), and only l1 reached the panel: a black grid.

kern.sweet_present_layers 1: SwapEnd completes the record with the layers it keeps; a frame of 2-4 live layers leaves
the direct scanout to presentGPU, which composites them with the 2D engine into the back panel buffer (layer 0 copied,
the others blended source-over, each scaled src rect -> dst rect), corner mattes over the panel corners, then the
normal 0905 flip. 8 GPU surface slots instead of 4 while on. Default 1 (2026-11-19, owner-tested); 0 = one layer only, as before.
Lines: `SWEET FB: 5s layers (1262)`; 1260's layout line gains each layer's flags `f F/U`.

